#!/usr/bin/env bash

HOOK_DIR="${BASH_SOURCE[0]%/*}"
if [[ "$HOOK_DIR" == "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}" ]]; then
  HOOK_DIR='.'
fi
ATCT_BIN="$HOOK_DIR/../bin/atct"
[[ -x "$ATCT_BIN" ]] || exit 0

CONTEXT_OUTPUT="$($ATCT_BIN context 2>/dev/null)" || exit 0
[[ -n "$CONTEXT_OUTPUT" ]] || exit 0

printf '%s\n' "$CONTEXT_OUTPUT"

/bin/cat <<'EOF'
This repository is registered with ATCT.
An active goal is permission to work. Declare tasks with `atct_task_declare`, claim one with `atct_task_claim`, and carry it through to a commit without waiting for approval to begin.
Finishing a task is not a checkpoint: claim the next one and keep going, moving to another active goal when this one has no unclaimed tasks left.
Stop only before what cannot be undone: rewriting history, discarding uncommitted work, deleting files, or publishing off this machine. Ask about those with `atct_decision_ask`.
When a choice would change the shape of the work, do not guess: `atct_decision_ask` with `wait_ms=0` parks it so you can keep going on something else.
An irreversible choice gets no `default_option`: park it, work on what does not depend on it, and let the human decide in their own time.
Answers from an earlier session arrive as `orphaned_decisions`; pass each `decision_id` to `atct_decision_poll`.
When the goal is met, call `atct_goal_complete` to request approval.
See the `atct` skill for details.
EOF
